    "title": "How to work the pipeline and convert leads",
    "summary": "Move deals through pipeline stages, convert a lead into an account, contact and opportunity, and record wins and losses.",
    "order": 4,
    "body": "\n## Move a lead through its statuses\n\nThe lead board has columns for new, contacted, qualified and converted. Drag a lead card from one column to the next as you work it, or use the list view with status filters and search.\n\n## Convert a lead\n\n1. Open the lead.\n2. Choose Convert.\n3. CRM creates an **account**, a **contact** and an **opportunity** in one step.\n\nFrom here the deal lives in the pipeline.\n\n## Work the pipeline\n\n- Use the pipeline **board** or **list**. Drag a deal between stages as it progresses.\n- Each opportunity has a **forecast category**: pipeline, best case, commit or closed. Weighted value is calculated from it.\n- Link the opportunity to an account, and add several contacts to the deal with a buying role such as decision maker or champion.\n- When a deal is lost, record the **loss reason**. It feeds the Win/Loss report.\n\n## Log your activity\n\nAdd calls, meetings, emails, notes and tasks to the lead, opportunity or account. Give a task to a teammate and they receive a notification. Everything appears on one timeline; an account's timeline rolls up its deals' and leads' activity.\n\n## Attach documents\n\nAttach files to leads, opportunities and accounts so the whole team can find them.\n",
