    "title": "How to control who sees what in CRM",
    "summary": "Use everyone, team and assigned-only access, assign and reassign leads, and file records to a team.",
    "order": 5,
    "body": "\nCRM lets you decide how much of the pipeline each person can see.\n\n## The three access levels\n\nFor each area (leads, pipeline, accounts and so on) a role can be set to:\n\n- **Everyone:** sees all records.\n- **Team:** a team lead sees their team's records.\n- **Assigned only:** a rep sees only their own records.\n\nRoles are customised in Settings → Roles & Permissions. See [Users, Roles, Teams & Permissions](/docs/start-here/users-roles-teams-permissions).\n\n## Assign and reassign leads\n\n1. Select one or more leads.\n2. Choose Assign and pick a person from the picker, which is grouped by team.\n3. Confirm. Every handover is recorded, and the supervisor of the team member who receives the work is notified.\n\n## File records to a team\n\nUse the bulk \"file to team\" action on leads, opportunities and accounts to move many records to a team at once.\n\n## Separate permissions\n\nLeads, pipeline, customers, reports (view and export) and integrations each have their own permission, so you can, for example, let someone see reports but not change integrations.\n",
